Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 04:53:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the release build, and point every link at anuragstpl
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The release workflow could never publish. Its Intel macOS job ran on macos-13,
which GitHub retired on 4 December 2025, so that leg failed immediately — and
because `publish` needed every platform, one dead runner image left the release
page empty even though the Windows build was fine.

- macos-13 -> macos-15-intel, macos-14 -> macos-15
- publish now runs if any platform succeeded, so a single broken runner ships
  the rest instead of blocking everything
- the publish job lists what it collected, so a partial release is obvious
- README, CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY, pyproject and the installer now point at
  github.com/anuragstpl/digital-assets-studio

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T37FTB9TMFqCFGZVfezhr8
---
 .github/workflows/release.yml | 16 ++++++++++++----
 CONTRIBUTING.md               |  2 +-
 README.md                     |  8 ++++----
 SECURITY.md                   |  2 +-
 packaging/installer.iss       |  2 +-
 packaging/set_repo.py         |  4 ++--
 pyproject.toml                |  6 +++---
 7 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/release.yml b/.github/workflows/release.yml
index 6e9bdd4..57d6c2c 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/release.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/release.yml
@@ -57,9 +57,10 @@ jobs:
       matrix:
         # arm64 for Apple silicon, x86_64 for Intel Macs
         include:
-          - runner: macos-14
+          - runner: macos-15
             arch: arm64
-          - runner: macos-13
+          # macos-13 was retired on 4 December 2025; macos-15-intel replaced it
+          - runner: macos-15-intel
             arch: x86_64
     runs-on: ${{ matrix.runner }}
     steps:
@@ -78,10 +79,17 @@ jobs:
   publish:
     needs: [windows, macos]
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
-    if: startsWith(github.ref, 'refs/tags/')
+    # `always()` so a failure on one platform still ships the others, rather than
+    # leaving the release page empty because a single runner image went away
+    if: always() && startsWith(github.ref, 'refs/tags/') && contains(needs.*.result, 'success')
     steps:
       - uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
-        with: {path: artifacts}
+        with:
+          path: artifacts
+          merge-multiple: false
+
+      - name: What was built
+        run: find artifacts -type f | sort
 
       - name: Publish the release
         uses: softprops/action-gh-release@v2
